--- candidate-03/critics/coverage_pair.jinja
+++ candidate-06/critics/coverage_pair.jinja
@@ -94,0 +95,8 @@
+Scope illustration using symbolic placeholders: let P be a generic stock
+paragraph already retained in the same complete notice. Copying that same P
+beneath a generic heading H is the covered-copy branch; heading adjacency alone
+does not turn P into a second independently stated obligation for H. This is
+different from an explicit additional assertion assigning H a particular state,
+condition or value V. Preserve that independent H/V assertion when the keeper
+lacks it. Test which of these two constructions is actually visible before
+applying general bound-subject or category-scope rules to a proposed loss.
@@ -126,0 +135,8 @@
+Operationally, compare the predicate separately from its qualified name slot:
+if the same short generic notice describes the same cookies/services behavior,
+adding, omitting or changing only its provider/recipient name stays within this
+finite exception. The grammatical object of an unchanged transfer clause is
+still such a recipient slot, not a new data flow by itself. Require an additional
+changed action, data type, restriction or condition to leave this branch. A bare
+section/navigation label contributes no unseen terms. Preserve actual liability,
+account-action destinations and independently changed processing facts.
